msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:16
msgid "Primitives"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:18
msgid "Integer"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:20
msgid "An _integer_ in the Nix language is a signed 64-bit integer."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:22
msgid ""
"Non-negative integers can be expressed as [integer literals](syntax."
"md#number-literal). Negative integers are created with the [arithmetic "
"negation operator](./operators.md#arithmetic). The function [`builtins."
"isInt`](builtins.md#builtins-isInt) can be used to determine if a value is "
"an integer."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:26
msgid "Float"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:28
msgid ""
"A _float_ in the Nix language is a 64-bit [IEEE 754](https://en.wikipedia."
"org/wiki/IEEE_754) floating-point number."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:30
msgid ""
"Most non-negative floats can be expressed as [float literals](syntax."
"md#number-literal). Negative floats are created with the [arithmetic "
"negation operator](./operators.md#arithmetic). The function [`builtins."
"isFloat`](builtins.md#builtins-isFloat) can be used to determine if a value "
"is a float."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:34
msgid "Boolean"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:36
msgid "A _boolean_ in the Nix language is one of _true_ or _false_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:40
msgid ""
"These values are available as attributes of [`builtins`](builtins."
"md#builtins-builtins) as [`builtins.true`](builtins.md#builtins-true) and "
"[`builtins.false`](builtins.md#builtins-false). The function [`builtins."
"isBool`](builtins.md#builtins-isBool) can be used to determine if a value is "
"a boolean."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:43
msgid "String"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:45
msgid ""
"A _string_ in the Nix language is an immutable, finite-length sequence of "
"bytes, along with a [string context](string-context.md). Nix does not assume "
"or support working natively with character encodings."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:48
msgid ""
"String values without string context can be expressed as [string literals]"
"(string-literals.md). The function [`builtins.isString`](builtins."
"md#builtins-isString) can be used to determine if a value is a string."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:51
msgid "Path"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:53
msgid ""
"A _path_ in the Nix language is an immutable, finite-length sequence of "
"bytes starting with `/`, representing a POSIX-style, canonical file system "
"path. Path values are distinct from string values, even if they contain the "
"same sequence of bytes. Operations that produce paths will simplify the "
"result as the standard C function [`realpath`](https://pubs.opengroup.org/"
"onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/realpath.html) would, except that there is "
"no symbolic link resolution."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:59
msgid ""
"Paths are suitable for referring to local files, and are often preferable "
"over strings."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:60
msgid "Path values do not contain trailing or duplicate slashes, `.`, or `..`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:61
msgid ""
"Relative path literals are automatically resolved relative to their [base "
"directory](../glossary.md#gloss-base-directory)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:62
msgid ""
"Tooling can recognize path literals and provide additional features, such as "
"autocompletion, refactoring automation and jump-to-file."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:66
msgid ""
"A file is not required to exist at a given path in order for that path value "
"to be valid, but a path that is converted to a string with [string "
"interpolation](string-interpolation.md#interpolated-expression) or [string-"
"and-path concatenation](operators.md#string-and-path-concatenation) must "
"resolve to a readable file or directory which will be copied into the Nix "
"store. For instance, evaluating `\"${./foo.txt}\"` will cause `foo.txt` from "
"the same directory to be copied into the Nix store and result in the string "
"`\"/nix/store/<hash>-foo.txt\"`. Operations such as [`import`](builtins."
"md#builtins-import) can also expect a path to resolve to a readable file or "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:74
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:76
msgid ""
"The Nix language assumes that all input files will remain _unchanged_ while "
"evaluating a Nix expression. For example, assume you used a file path in an "
"interpolated string during a `nix repl` session. Later in the same session, "
"after having changed the file contents, evaluating the interpolated string "
"with the file path again might not return a new [store path](../store/store-"
"path.md), since Nix might not re-read the file contents. Use `:r` to reset "
"the repl as needed."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:83
msgid ""
"Path values can be expressed as [path literals](syntax.md#path-literal). The "
"function [`builtins.isPath`](builtins.md#builtins-isPath) can be used to "
"determine if a value is a path."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:86
msgid "Null"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:88
msgid "There is a single value of type _null_ in the Nix language."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:92
msgid ""
"This value is available as an attribute on the [`builtins`](builtins."
"md#builtins-builtins) attribute set as [`builtins.null`](builtins."
"md#builtins-null)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:94
msgid "Compound values"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:96
msgid "Attribute set"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:100
msgid ""
"An attribute set can be constructed with an [attribute set literal](syntax."
"md#attrs-literal). The function [`builtins.isAttrs`](builtins.md#builtins-"
"isAttrs) can be used to determine if a value is an attribute set."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:103
msgid "List"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:107
msgid ""
"A list can be constructed with a [list literal](syntax.md#list-literal). The "
"function [`builtins.isList`](builtins.md#builtins-isList) can be used to "
"determine if a value is a list."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:110
msgid "Function"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:114
msgid ""
"A function can be constructed with a [function expression](syntax."
"md#functions). The function [`builtins.isFunction`](builtins.md#builtins-"
"isFunction) can be used to determine if a value is a function."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:117
msgid "External"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/types.md:119
msgid ""
"An _external_ value is an opaque value created by a Nix [plugin](../command-"
"ref/conf-file.md#conf-plugin-files). Such a value can be substituted in Nix "
"expressions but only created and used by plugin code."
msgstr ""
